--TEST--
the class `Core\Test::assertThrows` expects is an error, so its literal is offered the classes that are a `Throwable`: the error classes the language declares and the program's own, and no other class — `rule:types/class-reference`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Cart { }
class OutOfStock extends RuntimeError { }

Core\Test::assertThrows(fn (): void => { }, '<|>');
--REQUEST--
completion
--EXPECT--
ArithmeticError class
Core\Cli\NotInteractive class
Core\Db\DbError class
Core\Db\RolledBack class
Core\Test\Failure class
IOError class
LogicError class
OutOfStock class
ParseError class
RecursionError class
RuntimeError class
Throwable class
TimeoutError class
